            { text: "And both are rational, therefore {GD|DG} and {DF} are rational straight lines commensurable in square only.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["DG","DF"] },
            { text: "Therefore {FG} is an apotome.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["FG"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "FG an apotome", ref: "X.73" }] },
            { text: "And {FH} is rational, but the rectangle contained by a rational straight line and an apotome is irrational,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["FH","FG","FEh"] },
            { text: "and its side is irrational.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["FEh"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "FE and its side irrational", ref: "X.20" }] },
            { text: "And {AC} is the side of {FE|FEh}, therefore {AC} is irrational.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AC","FEh"] },
            { text: "Let it be called that which produces with a medial area a medial whole.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AC"],
